Stat 5810 Applied Spatial Statistics                                 Fall 2000

         Analysis of the Volcanic Craters Data by Bailey/Gatrell
         =======================================================

                        Wed 10/11/00 & Mon 10/16/00 


Dr. Juergen Symanzik

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) Load the volcanic craters data from the Web, i.e., from
  http://math.usu.edu/~symanzik/teaching/2000_spatial/infomap_data/Volcano.txt
Store it locally in a file.
Open the file in a text editor. 
Remove the headings and the "'" symbols. 
Then store the data set locally.


2) Reading in the Data and Creating a SPP:

vol _ matrix( scan ("/home/symanzik/splus/Volcano.dat"), 120, 4, byrow = T)
vol.coord _ matrix( c(vol[,2], vol[,3]), 120, 2)
vol.spp _ spp (vol.coord)
summary (vol.spp)


3) Simple Plots: Data and Kernel Estimates

par (mfrow = c(2,2))
par (pty = "s")
plot (vol.spp, main = "Volcanic Craters")
   # should be similar to Figure 3.1 in Bailey/Gatrell

vol.kernel100 _ intensity (vol.spp, method = "kernel", bw = 100)
image (vol.kernel100)

vol.kernel220 _ intensity (vol.spp, method = "kernel", bw = 220)
image (vol.kernel220)

vol.kernel500 _ intensity (vol.spp, method = "kernel", bw = 500)
image (vol.kernel500)
   # should be similar to Figure 3.5 in Bailey/Gatrell


4) Nearest Neighbor Plots, Khat & Lhat function:

par (mfrow = c(2,2))
vol.ghat _ Ghat (vol.spp)
   # should be similar to Figure 3.6 in Bailey/Gatrell
vol.khat _ Khat (vol.spp)
vol.lhat _ Lhat (vol.spp)
abline(0, 1)
   # positive peaks between 100 and 1500 - probably clustering!


5) Khat and Simulation Envelopes:

par (mfrow = c(1,2))

vol.khat _ Khat (vol.spp, plot = F)
plot (vol.khat$values[vol.khat$values[,1] < 500, ])
title ("Khat & Simulation Envelopes, dist < 500")

vol.kenv _ Kenv (vol.spp, nsims = 39, add = F)
vol.index _ vol.kenv$dist < 500
lines (vol.kenv$dist[vol.index], vol.kenv$lower[vol.index])
lines (vol.kenv$dist[vol.index], vol.kenv$upper[vol.index])
   # if there was any doubt - certainly clustering at these distances!


plot (vol.khat$values[vol.khat$values[,1] < 100, ])
title ("Khat & Simulation Envelopes, dist < 100")

vol.index _ vol.kenv$dist < 100
lines (vol.kenv$dist[vol.index], vol.kenv$lower[vol.index])
lines (vol.kenv$dist[vol.index], vol.kenv$upper[vol.index])
   # regularity not very likely at small distances!


